Reason:
The fix adds a `max` parameter to the function and checks if the index `n` has reached the maximum before writing. Callers now pass the available size of the array minus one (to reserve one slot for the ingress device index). If the number of upper devices exceeds the limit, the function returns -EOVERFLOW, and the caller aborts the redirect, preventing the out-of-bounds write.

